title: LSP Diagnostics

The editor marks links and transclusions whose target does not exist, through `textDocument/publishDiagnostics`. Try it in [[LSP Diagnostics - (Example)]].

!! When diagnostics are recomputed

Not on every keystroke. Warnings are recomputed once typing pauses for about a third of a second, so a link you are halfway through writing is not squiggled while you write it. Opening a document reports immediately; closing one clears its warnings and cancels any pass still waiting.

!! What is not flagged

A link is left alone when it is an external address, inside any filter (a filtered transclusion, a filter attribute, an `<%if%>` condition or a `\function` body, where `[[X]]` names a title rather than linking to it), inside inline code or a fenced block, or in the field header of a `.tid` file, where a `tags` field routinely names tiddlers that do not exist yet.

A target assembled at render time from a variable cannot be checked at all, so it is never reported.
